Fixture quarantine: excluded from build/test execution and the new CMake/Ninja build

These are not deferred tests that run anyway. The existing fixture selector refuses
them, CI selection withholds them, and Gradle excludes their consumer classes in
all modes. The existing selection manifest carries quarantined=true on each named
group. The blanket preparation entry point now stops without running producers.
Do not register these producers or consumers in the new CMake/Ninja graph.
Direct producer commands remain source material for isolated repair, not build
entry points. No fixture generation is being run during this inventory.

Readmission requires useful semantic coverage, named file inputs, one producer
per output file, and successful incremental regeneration without clearing a
published output directory or reading a previous attempt. Keep private scratch
files separate. A producer may have several declared outputs; an output may not
have several producers. Exact compiler counts and historical receipts do not
justify preserving a fixture.

Previous attempts affect output names or are prerequisites:
  simd-int32x4-bytearray (030), simd-word32x4-bytearray (031),
  simd-floatx4-bytearray (032), simd-doublex2-bytearray (033): copy every old
    receipt artifact before generation; missing old files block replacement;
    random attempt directories become published inputs.
  boxed-cas (044), boxed-array-extensions (049), original-stack (098): select
    run-N using existing directories; move/archive previous manifests.

Unrelated directory members change consumed inputs or make generation fail:
  bytearray (018), mutable-bytearrays (019), resize-bytearrays (020),
  mutable-bytearray-size (021), compare-byte-arrays (022): consume every stage CBD.
  simd-address-families (027): manifest collects generated source/*.hs leftovers.
  data-to-tag (039), proxy-void (042): consume all CBDs found in the output tree.
  fetch-add-int-array (045), atomic-int-arrays (046), shrink-bytearrays (047),
    mutvar (081): exact output-directory inventories reject unrelated CBDs.
  floating-tuples (086), sum-results (088), tuple-input (114),
    empty-tuple-input (126), show-word-list (127), state-tuple (128),
    short-bytes-slices (129), tuple-return (130), unsafe-equality (134),
    tag-to-enum (135): recursively discovered products enter receipts consumed
    by tests. sum-results includes aggregate-layout, sum-layout and sum-result.
  compiled-thunk-retention (097): boxed-array producer consumes every stage CBD;
    its grouped consumers include the floating fixture. Split useful independent
    coverage before admitting it separately.
  array-slices (123): consumes every stage CBD and also rewrites shared coverage.

Published directories are cleared as part of the recipe:
  sqrt (026): removes build/sqrt.
  address-identity (101): removes build/addr-identity.
  synchronous-exceptions (103): selection/default script removes its output tree;
    producer also enumerates stage CBDs.
  corpus (119): removes group output directories before export.
  managed-mvars (133): selected --refresh deletes the output tree.

Joint output ownership:
  cbv-coercion (014): independently produces tuple-arithmetic's pre CBD and an
    explicit64-primops CBD. The owning arithmetic producers must be the sole
    writers; a consumer needing those files must depend on their producers.
  mutable-bytearrays (019), resize-bytearrays (020), mutable-bytearray-size (021),
    array-slices (123): regenerate build/primop-coverage.json from inside recipes.
    Shared coverage must have one separate owning rule.
  backend-annotations (040): independently publishes build/thc-fixtures.path,
    also published by compact-model and common/default setup. The backend fixture
    must consume the encoder from one shared owner instead.
  simd-capability-smoke (116): invokes the generator that also writes application
    Java/fixture sources through Gradle. The generator needs one owner and the
    fixture must consume the generated sources, not regenerate them.

Shared infrastructure also excluded from translation as fixture rules:
  fast_fixtures.py full receipt: recursive output inventory and top-level build/
    allowlist make unrelated outputs affect reuse. Do not port this behavior.
  prepare-tests.sh: blanket ordered preparation, cleanup commands, repeated shared
    publication and metadata checks with undeclared outputs. Do not wrap this in
    one CMake preparation target. Replace it with admitted file-producing rules.

Not quarantined merely for this reason:
  Test-private filesystem state used to check unlink/rename/directory semantics.
  A shared tool called by several rules, provided its products have ONE owning
    rule and callers only consume those products.
  The application runtime's native providers are Gradle-owned application products,
    not fixture admission decisions. Their incrementality defects are recorded in
    fixture-inputs.log's shared appendix and still need repair at their owner.
